#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Move JPEG encoding off HPWORK onto a dedicated low-priority thread.

Measured on hardware: one 320x240 frame takes about 766 ms of pure DCT and
Huffman work.  Running that on HPWORK (priority 224) starved the CP-side IPC
heartbeat thread (priority 100, kthread_create in bk7258_pm_pwc.c:205); two
frames fit inside the 2 s heartbeat window, the third did not, and CP asserted
at mb_ipc_task:297 and reset the board.

The same failure mode is already documented in bk7258_yuv_buf.c:301, where an
ISR-side printf starved task-level work until the heartbeat asserted.  Long
computation simply must not sit above the heartbeat.

HPWORK exists for interrupt bottom halves -- short, latency-sensitive work.
LPWORK would also outrank the heartbeat by default and is shared with other
subsystems, so instead this uses one dedicated thread whose priority is
explicitly below the heartbeat's.  A codec that falls behind then just encodes
slower, which is the correct failure mode.
"""

import sys

P = ("/home/mi/vela_competition_ap_console_dev/contest/"
     "contest2026_264_VelaSightsuixingAIzhinengyanjing/board/beken/boards/"
     "bk7258/bk7258-ap/src/bk7258_jpeg_enc.c")

src = open(P).read()
edits = []


def sub(old, new, label):
    global src
    n = src.count(old)
    if n != 1:
        print("FAIL [%s]: found %d, expected 1" % (label, n))
        sys.exit(1)
    src = src.replace(old, new, 1)
    edits.append(label)


