Software JPEG runs about 11 us per pixel on this part -- 820 ms for 320x240,
so 640x480 needs well over three seconds and the flat timeout gave up before
the first frame ever arrived.  Budget 40 us per pixel plus a floor, which
leaves generous headroom while still being bounded: a wedged driver must not
hang the shell forever.
"""

import sys

