#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Accept the camera's actual byte order, and encode out of the encode pool.

Two changes, both needed before a captured frame can be encoded correctly.

The camera's frames are tagged V4L2_PIX_FMT_UYVY but YUV_BUF writes the four
bus bytes of each pixel pair backwards, so memory holds Cr Y1 Cb Y0 rather
than textbook Cb Y0 Cr Y1 (measured in bk7258_camera_imgsensor.c, and used by
camera_preview's g_orders[] table).  Reading such a frame as UYVY exchanges
